      <h2>Emergency Plumber Huyton. Your Questions Answered</h2>
      <div class="pf-faq">
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">COST</span>&nbsp; How much does an emergency plumber cost in Huyton?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>£120 for the first hour on weekdays 9am to 4pm. £150 for the first hour on weekday evenings, nights and weekends. £180 for the first hour on bank holidays. Extra time is priced before we carry on. Parts at cost. Most jobs cost £120 to £350 total. Written quote before work starts. No call-out fee.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">RESPONSE</span>&nbsp; How quickly can you reach Huyton?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>We're based in Kirkby. Huyton is a 15 minute run via the M57. We guarantee a 30 minute response. A real person picks up the phone any time of day or night.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">LOCAL</span>&nbsp; Are you a local Knowsley plumber?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. We're at 29 Park Road, Kirkby, L32 2AL. Same Knowsley Council as Huyton. The other plumbers ranking for emergency plumber Huyton are based in Liverpool, Lancashire or run national call centres. We're the local Knowsley team.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">SEMIS</span>&nbsp; Do you work on the old council-built semis?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. The 1950s and 1960s council-built semis are the bulk of Huyton stock. Most have been bought through right-to-buy and upgraded over decades. We know the typical pipe layouts. We carry common parts on the van.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-green">OLD BOILER</span>&nbsp; My boiler is over 20 years old. Should I repair or replace?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>A boiler over 20 years old with regular faults is almost always cheaper to replace than to repair. Parts get hard to find. Old boilers run at 70 to 75% efficiency. A modern combi runs at 92 to 94%. A new boiler from £2,195 pays for itself in lower gas bills inside 7 to 10 years.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">AREAS</span>&nbsp; Do you cover Stockbridge Village and Page Moss?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Stockbridge Village, Page Moss, Court Hey, Bakers Green, Roby and the rest of L36 are all covered at the same fixed rates. Same 15 minute response from Kirkby.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">GAS SAFE</span>&nbsp; Are your engineers Gas Safe registered?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. All gas work is done by our Gas Safe registered engineers. Check our entry at <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gassaferegister.co.uk</a>. It's against the law to work on gas without it.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">GUARANTEE</span>&nbsp; Do you guarantee your work?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Every job has a 12-month workmanship guarantee. If something we fixed fails because of our work, we come back. No charge.</p></div></details>
